From f797708c0626e5f9840ca5b0a98790e2c7cb09ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Lzy <davidli@localhost>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] amd: use gfx9 DPP broadcast for Vega20 reductions

The established gfx906 Triton 3.6 path treats Vega20 as a DPP-capable
CDNA-style target. Triton 3.7 introduced a narrower feature helper but omitted
the newly registered family, which sent full-wave reductions through the RDNA
permlanex16 lowering. gfx906 cannot select that intrinsic. Keep the validated
DPP broadcast path for Vega20.

---
 third_party/amd/lib/TritonAMDGPUToLLVM/TargetInfo.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/third_party/amd/lib/TritonAMDGPUToLLVM/TargetInfo.cpp b/third_party/amd/lib/TritonAMDGPUToLLVM/TargetInfo.cpp
index a906fa9..2456707 100644
--- a/third_party/amd/lib/TritonAMDGPUToLLVM/TargetInfo.cpp
+++ b/third_party/amd/lib/TritonAMDGPUToLLVM/TargetInfo.cpp
@@ -744,6 +744,7 @@ void TargetInfo::localLoadOpAnnotation(triton::gpu::LocalLoadOp localLoadOp,
 
 bool TargetInfo::supportDppBroadcast() const {
   switch (getISAFamily()) {
+  case ISAFamily::VEGA20:
   case ISAFamily::CDNA1:
   case ISAFamily::CDNA2:
   case ISAFamily::CDNA3:
-- 
